      "name": "smart-guideline-end-to-end",
      "title": "smart-guideline-end-to-end",
      "description": "The whole road from a use case to a running application on WHO SMART Guidelines, for a new guideline or a jurisdiction's adaptation, as an orchestrator of ten named stage skills, each with its own input and output contract: guideline-use-case, dak-l1-library, recommendation-extraction, l2-dependency-choice, l2-dak-authoring, l3-dependency-choice, l3-fhir-authoring, l4-application-brief, wireframe-design-review and l4-application-build. Each stage's output is the next stage's input. Human adjudication follows every stage, as QA and never as a gate: the agent goes on to the next stage while the last one is reviewed. The ORDER of the stages is a rule, though: no L3 asset before the L1 extraction and the L2 assets it derives from exist and their review has been requested. Read before starting any end-to-end authoring or adaptation, and to find which skill runs each stage. A request to adapt a WHO guideline, DAK or IG to a country or programme (\"adapt the immunization guidelines to Uganda using these schedules\") is this process, even when it reads like an IG or coding task.",
      "instructionsPath": "skills/content/authoring-who-smart-guidelines/smart-guideline-end-to-end.md",
